["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Every white tail you ever get close to, you got close by beating its nose, ears and eyes in that order.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A deer's senses ranked. 1, nose: strongest, catches your scent far downwind, only the wind beats it. 2, ears: high clicks, zips, nylon and voices, beat it with quiet gear and slow feet. 3, eyes: motion and outline, not colour detail, beat it with stillness and a background. Bar lengths show rank, not measured distance.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Nose, then ears, then eyes</text>\n  <g font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"76\">1 Nose</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"146\">2 Ears</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"216\">3 Eyes</text></g>\n  <rect x=\"100\" y=\"56\" width=\"285\" height=\"28\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <rect x=\"100\" y=\"126\" width=\"210\" height=\"28\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f2a56b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"100\" y=\"196\" width=\"150\" height=\"28\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\"><text x=\"110\" y=\"76\">never lies</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"146\">metal, zips</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"216\">motion</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"104\">Beat it: only with the wind</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"174\">Beat it: quiet gear, slow feet</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"244\">Beat it: freeze, have a background</text></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bars show rank, not distance (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Nose first, ears second, eyes third (Tip, ranking).</li><li>Valley white tails live where wind swirls and air pools (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what this chapter covers</summary><ul><li>Nose and how scent travels with wind and thermals.</li><li>Ears: what they hear best.</li><li>Eyes: colour, motion, low light, field of view.</li><li>How a white tail combines the three, and how to beat each one.</li><li>Shared deer sense biology is also in <a href=\"#/s/mc-mule-deer-03\">Mule deer Masterclass 3</a>, <a href=\"#/s/deer-mind\">How a deer thinks</a> and <a href=\"#/s/wind-thermals\">Wind and thermals</a>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, top view. Wind blows left to right. A hunter stands on the left and an orange scent cone spreads out downwind, getting wider with distance. A deer walks up from the bottom right into the cone and stops: it smells the hunter. Another deer upwind of the hunter, on the lower left, is safe.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Your scent cone grows downwind</text><g><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"44\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"44\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"70.0,44.0 61.9,47.9 61.9,40.1\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;16 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><g><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"74\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"70.0,74.0 61.9,77.9 61.9,70.1\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;16 0;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></g><text x=\"22\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">Wind</text><path d=\"M110 150 L390 70 L390 230 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;.22\" dur=\"2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path><path d=\"M110 150 L250 112 L250 188 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;.25\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"1s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></path><circle cx=\"110\" cy=\"140.0\" r=\"7.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"103.0\" y=\"148.0\" width=\"14.0\" height=\"20.0\" rx=\"4.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">You</text><path id=\"mwt-scent-cone-p1\" d=\"M330 290 L330 196\" fill=\"none\"/><g><g transform=\"translate(0 0) rotate(-90)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"0\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M19 -4 l6 -6 M19 4 l6 6\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><animateMotion dur=\"5s\" fill=\"freeze\"><mpath href=\"#mwt-scent-cone-p1\"/></animateMotion></g><g opacity=\"0\"><text x=\"330\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Smells you!</text><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"5s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></g><g><g transform=\"translate(60 260) rotate(-60)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"0\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M19 -4 l6 -6 M19 4 l6 6\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g></g><text x=\"60\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Upwind: safe</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Scent cone</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Your scent spreads in a cone downwind. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Smell is its strongest sense <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Your scent fans out downwind, wider with distance <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: nose detail</summary><ul><li>A deer's nose is its best sense <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. The often quoted \"297 million receptors\" is folklore (45%, not a fact).</li><li>Your scent comes from breath, skin, clothes, boots and your truck (Tip).</li><li>It spreads downwind as a <strong>cone</strong>: narrow at you, wide far away (80%, physics of drifting air).</li><li>Light wind swirls the cone. Steady wind keeps it tight and predictable (Tip).</li><li>White tails often bed and travel so the wind brings them news from where they cannot see (Tip, hunter observation).</li><li>The Hunt Map has a <strong>Scent cone</strong> tool: set the wind and see where your scent goes (<a href=\"#/map\">Hunt Map</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Your scent cone. Wind carries scent from your breath, skin, clothes and boots in a widening cone downwind. A deer standing in the cone smells you. A deer upwind or off to the side of the cone does not. Your truck leaves scent too.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Your scent cone</text>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"220\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <path d=\"M70 150 L390 60 L390 240 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".18\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M20 60 H90 m-12 -8 l12 8 l-12 8\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">Wind</text>\n  <circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"150\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(320 160)\"><ellipse rx=\"18\" ry=\"9\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-16\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">smells you</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(250 255)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-14\" cy=\"-7\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">safe: outside the cone</text>\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">breath, skin,</text>\n  <text x=\"150\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">clothes, boots</text>\n</svg>\n</figure>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation, valley cross section in the evening. Cool air slides down both slopes into the river bottom, shown as moving dots. Orange dots from a hunter on the left slope carry the hunter&#x27;s scent down to a deer bedded in the willows by the river.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Evening: cold air drains to the river</text><path d=\"M0 70 L120 210 L160 240 L240 240 L280 210 L400 70 L400 300 L0 300 Z\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"170\" y=\"236\" width=\"60\" height=\"8\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">River bottom</text><polygon points=\"140,194.8 129.6,222 150.4,222\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"138.0\" y=\"222\" width=\"4.0\" height=\"6.4\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><polygon points=\"258,194.8 247.6,222 268.4,222\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><rect x=\"256.0\" y=\"222\" width=\"4.0\" height=\"6.4\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><ellipse cx=\"196\" cy=\"228\" rx=\"12.8\" ry=\"8.0\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><ellipse cx=\"204.0\" cy=\"223.2\" rx=\"8.8\" ry=\"6.4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><g transform=\"translate(232 226) rotate(0)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"17\" cy=\"0\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M19 -4 l6 -6 M19 4 l6 6\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"114.0\" r=\"7.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"73.0\" y=\"122.0\" width=\"14.0\" height=\"20.0\" rx=\"4.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">You</text><path id=\"mwt-valley-drain-p1\" d=\"M90 120 L150 200 L200 226\" fill=\"none\"/><path id=\"mwt-valley-drain-p2\" d=\"M320 110 L262 196 L210 226\" fill=\"none\"/><circle r=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".8\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" begin=\"0s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"><mpath href=\"#mwt-valley-drain-p1\"/></animateMotion></circle><circle r=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" begin=\"0.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"><mpath href=\"#mwt-valley-drain-p2\"/></animateMotion></circle><circle r=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".8\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" begin=\"1s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"><mpath href=\"#mwt-valley-drain-p1\"/></animateMotion></circle><circle r=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" begin=\"1.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"><mpath href=\"#mwt-valley-drain-p2\"/></animateMotion></circle><circle r=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".8\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" begin=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"><mpath href=\"#mwt-valley-drain-p1\"/></animateMotion></circle><circle r=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" begin=\"2.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"><mpath href=\"#mwt-valley-drain-p2\"/></animateMotion></circle><circle r=\"5\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".8\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" begin=\"3s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"><mpath href=\"#mwt-valley-drain-p1\"/></animateMotion></circle><circle r=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" opacity=\".7\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" begin=\"3.5s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"><mpath href=\"#mwt-valley-drain-p2\"/></animateMotion></circle><text x=\"330\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Cool air sinks</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Your scent rides it down to the deer.</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Evening: cool air slides down to the river. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Evening: cool air drains downhill to the bottoms <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Morning sun: air rises up the slopes <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: thermals for white tail country</summary><ul><li>Sun warms slopes in the morning, warm air rises, scent drifts <strong>uphill</strong> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Slopes cool in the evening, cool air sinks, scent drifts <strong>downhill</strong> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>In a valley, that cool air pools along the river at dusk and dawn, right where white tails bed in willow and cottonwood (Tip, from thermal physics).</li><li>So an evening stand on the slope above a river bottom can leak your scent down to the deer (Tip).</li><li>Better: sit on the field edge with the bottom upwind, or on the bottom's downwind side (Tip).</li><li>At dawn before sun hits, air still sinks. It flips once the slope warms <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of thermals on a slope. Morning: the sun rises and warms the slope, warm air rises, and scent drifts uphill, so approach from above or the side. Evening: the sun sets, the slope cools, cool air sinks, and scent drifts downhill, so hunt from below or the side and leave before cold air drains your scent down to bedded deer.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dbe7f3\"/>\n  <circle r=\"18\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" cx=\"40\" cy=\"250\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"250;70;70;250\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;0.6;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <animate attributeName=\"cx\" values=\"40;80;330;370\" keyTimes=\"0;0.3;0.6;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <animate attributeName=\"fill\" values=\"#f3d36b;#f3d36b;#f2a56b;#e8590c\" keyTimes=\"0;0.5;0.8;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n  </circle>\n  <path d=\"M0 290 L0 260 Q150 240 260 120 Q300 80 400 60 L400 290 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <g transform=\"translate(220 160)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-14\" cy=\"-7\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.1;0.5;0.55;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M90 250 Q150 220 200 175 m-14 2 l14 -2 l-2 14\"/>\n    <path d=\"M150 260 Q220 210 270 140 m-14 2 l14 -2 l-2 14\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\"0\">\n    <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.6;0.65;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <path d=\"M270 120 Q220 190 160 235 m2 -14 l-2 14 l14 0\"/>\n    <path d=\"M330 100 Q280 170 230 215 m2 -14 l-2 14 l14 0\"/>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"36\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Morning: warm air, scent goes UP\n    <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"0\" begin=\"4.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" opacity=\"0\">Evening: cool air, scent sinks DOWN\n    <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"4.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.05;0.9;1\" begin=\"1.5s\" dur=\"3.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"96\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You: above</text></g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" from=\"0\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"262\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">You: below</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Morning scent rises, evening scent sinks. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Deer hearing chart. Deer hear from about 115 hertz to 54 kilohertz, best around 4 to 8 kilohertz. Zippers, Velcro, nylon swish, metal on metal and snapping twigs all sit in that best band.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<line x1=\"30\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"30\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 Hz</text>\n<line x1=\"156\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"156\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"156\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 kHz</text>\n<line x1=\"282\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"282\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"282\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10 kHz</text>\n<line x1=\"370\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"370\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50 kHz</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What a deer hears best</text>\n\n<rect x=\"38\" y=\"70\" width=\"337\" height=\"36\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"46\" y=\"94\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\">Deer: 115 Hz to 54 kHz</text>\n<rect x=\"232\" y=\"116\" width=\"38\" height=\"36\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">best: 4 to 8 kHz</text>\n<path d=\"M250 178 V200\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"20\" y=\"200\" width=\"360\" height=\"86\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f6dccb\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">In the danger band:</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">zippers, Velcro, nylon swish,</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">metal on metal, snapping twigs</text>\n</svg></figure><ul><li>Hears about 115 Hz (hertz) to 54 kHz (kilohertz) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Best at 4 to 8 kHz: zippers, Velcro, metal clicks <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: ears detail</summary><ul><li>Deer hear from about 115 Hz (hertz) to 54 kHz (kilohertz), best around 4 to 8 kHz (85%, D'Angelo and others 2007).</li><li>That best band is exactly zippers, Velcro, nylon swish, metal on metal and snapping twigs <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Each ear swivels on its own to point at a sound <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Natural rhythms (a squirrel, another deer: step, stop, step) pass. Steady two legged crunching does not (Tip).</li><li>Idaho Fish and Game: white tails have very good hearing for danger and give a loud snort when alarmed <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a deer with its field of view. Green covers about 310 degrees around it: it sees to the sides and almost behind without turning its head. A narrow orange wedge in front is where both eyes overlap and judge depth. A small brown wedge straight behind is the blind spot.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What a deer sees from one spot</text><path d=\"M200 160 L249.9 266.9 A 118 118 0 1 0 150.1 266.9 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".45\"/><path d=\"M200 160 L150.1 53.1 A 118 118 0 0 1 249.9 53.1 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".35\"/><path d=\"M200 160 L249.9 266.9 A 118 118 0 0 1 150.1 266.9 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><g transform=\"translate(200 160)\"><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"24\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cy=\"-26\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-7\" cy=\"-26\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"-26\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Both eyes: depth</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Side vision</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Side vision</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Blind behind</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">About 310 degrees without moving the head.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Sees about 310 degrees without turning its head <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Poor depth and detail; great at motion <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: field of view detail</summary><ul><li>Eyes on the sides of the head give about a 310 degree view (80%, Penn State Deer Research; some sources say 300).</li><li>The blind spot is a narrow wedge straight behind <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Only a narrow zone in front is seen by both eyes, so depth judgement is poor <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Horizontal pupil</strong>: a wide slit that scans the horizon, typical of prey animals <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Rods give strong motion detection and good low light vision <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>A reflective layer behind the retina (tapetum lucidum) brightens dim light. That is the eye shine in headlights <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 320\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How a deer sees colour, a rough picture. Deer have two colour cones, blue near 455 nanometres and green near 537, and no red cone. Blaze orange looks dull, close to grey or brown. Blue stands out. Some detergent brighteners may glow in ultraviolet. Motion and outline give you away, not colour.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"320\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You see / a deer sees</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><text x=\"14\" y=\"82\">You</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"162\">Deer</text></g>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"55\" width=\"70\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ff6a00\"/><rect x=\"160\" y=\"55\" width=\"70\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4f7f3a\"/><rect x=\"240\" y=\"55\" width=\"70\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f63c9\"/><rect x=\"320\" y=\"55\" width=\"66\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#f2f2f2\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"135\" width=\"70\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#9c9478\"/><rect x=\"160\" y=\"135\" width=\"70\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#7f8a6a\"/><rect x=\"240\" y=\"135\" width=\"70\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#2f63e0\"/><rect x=\"320\" y=\"135\" width=\"66\" height=\"44\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#d8e6ff\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"115\" y=\"120\">orange</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"120\">green</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"120\">blue</text><text x=\"353\" y=\"120\">bright wash</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"115\" y=\"200\">dull</text><text x=\"195\" y=\"200\">greyer</text><text x=\"275\" y=\"200\">stands out</text><text x=\"353\" y=\"200\">UV glow?</text></g>\n  <rect x=\"14\" y=\"222\" width=\"372\" height=\"86\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Colour is not the problem.</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#f3d36b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Motion and outline are.</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"298\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rough picture, not exact colours (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>No red cone: blaze orange looks dull <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><ul><li>Motion and outline give you away <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: colour detail</summary><ul><li>Deer have 2 colour cones, peaking near 455 nm (blue) and 537 nm (green). No red cone (85%, Jacobs and others 1994).</li><li>So blaze orange looks dull, close to grey or brown <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Blue stands out more (65%, Tip: skip blue jeans).</li><li>In low light, deer are most sensitive to blue and blue green (80%, Penn State).</li><li>Deer see more ultraviolet (UV) than we do <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Unscented soap without UV brighteners (Tip, 65%).</li><li>A moving phone screen or headlamp in the dark is pure motion (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"gallery\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-doe.jpg\" alt=\"A doe at full alert: ears and eyes on you.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>A doe at full alert: ears and eyes on you. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: U.S. Fish and Wildlife Service - Midwest Region, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:White-tailed_deer_(54365597311).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/g-wt-buck-front.jpg\" alt=\"Head on: both eyes forward, the only depth zone.\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Head on: both eyes forward, the only depth zone. <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Famartin, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2024-11-08_10_54_30_White-tailed_Deer_buck_along_Montague_Avenue_in_the_Mountainview_section_of_Ewing_Township,_Mercer_County,_New_Jersey.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure></div>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Side view. A white tail scans along the horizon, shown as an orange band at its own eye level. A hunter on the ground is inside the band. A hunter sitting in a tree stand is above it. Caption: deer do look up; height plus stillness helps. Labelled as a tip.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Get out of the eye line (Tip)</text><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><g transform=\"translate(300 200) scale(0.8 0.8)\"><rect x=\"-41\" y=\"12\" width=\"6\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"-31\" y=\"12\" width=\"6\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"27\" y=\"12\" width=\"6\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><rect x=\"37\" y=\"12\" width=\"6\" height=\"40\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"52\" ry=\"22\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-30 -10 L-52 -42 L-40 -48 L-18 -14 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cx=\"-58\" cy=\"-46\" rx=\"15\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-50 -52 L-44 -64 L-40 -52 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-64\" cy=\"-47\" r=\"1.8\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><path d=\"M50 -8 C 60 -6 64 6 60 18 C 54 16 50 6 48 -2 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/></g><path d=\"M253 162 L20 140 L20 230 L253 172 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".18\"/><text x=\"110\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Main view: level</text><rect x=\"90\" y=\"70\" width=\"8\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"86\" width=\"40\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"84\" cy=\"64.2\" r=\"6.3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"77.7\" y=\"71.4\" width=\"12.6\" height=\"18.0\" rx=\"3.6\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"140\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Up a tree stand</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"206.0\" r=\"7.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"33.0\" y=\"214.0\" width=\"14.0\" height=\"20.0\" rx=\"4.0\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ground</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Deer do look up. Height plus stillness helps.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Height takes you out of the main view (Tip).</li><li>Deer do look up. Stillness still matters most (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: stands and eye level</summary><ul><li>A white tail scans the horizon at its own eye level (80%, horizontal pupil).</li><li>A tree stand or a ground blind with a dark back wall hides your outline (Tip, hunter consensus).</li><li>Ground hunters: sit in shadow with something behind you, not on the skyline (Tip).</li><li>Deer that have been hunted from stands learn to look up (Tip).</li><li>Tree stand safety: wear a full body harness and stay clipped in from the ground up (Tip, widely taught tree stand safety). Ground blinds avoid the fall risk (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Flow chart. A white tail hears an odd sound, lifts its head and stares. If it sees motion it stamps or head bobs. If it is still not sure it often circles downwind to smell, which is a hunter tip. When the nose confirms danger it snorts, flags and leaves.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">How a white tail checks a threat</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"40\" width=\"200\" height=\"44\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"68\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Ears: odd sound</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"100\" width=\"200\" height=\"44\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"128\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Head up, eyes lock on</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"160\" width=\"200\" height=\"44\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"188\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Motion? Stamp, bob</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"220\" width=\"200\" height=\"44\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"248\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Not sure? Circles</text><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"130.0,98.0 126.1,89.9 133.9,89.9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"144\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"158\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"130.0,158.0 126.1,149.9 133.9,149.9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"204\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"218\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"130.0,218.0 126.1,209.9 133.9,209.9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><rect x=\"250\" y=\"210\" width=\"140\" height=\"60\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fbe3d4\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Nose confirms:</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">snort, flag, gone</text><line x1=\"232\" y1=\"242\" x2=\"248\" y2=\"242\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"248.0,242.0 239.9,245.9 239.9,238.1\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">downwind to</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"88\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">smell you (Tip)</text><path d=\"M232 236 C 300 230 330 160 320 98\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"292\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ears and eyes raise doubt. The nose decides.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Ears and eyes raise doubt. The nose decides (Tip).</li><li>Unsure white tails often circle downwind (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how they combine</summary><ul><li>A white tail often hears you first, then looks for motion (Tip, hunter observation).</li><li>If it sees something odd but cannot smell it, it may stamp, head bob or stare to make you move <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Many hunters report unsure white tails circling to get downwind (Tip, widely reported, not measured).</li><li>Once the nose confirms: snort, flag, gone <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>The full alarm ladder (alert, head bob, stamp, snort, run) is in <a href=\"#/s/deer-mind\">How a deer thinks</a> and chapter 4.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Sense</th><th>Beat it with</th><th>Never</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Nose</td><td>Wind and thermals <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td><td>Hunt a bad wind (Tip)</td></tr><tr><td>Ears</td><td>Wool, slow feet (Tip)</td><td>Zippers, Velcro <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Eyes</td><td>Stillness, shade <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td><td>Skyline, quick moves (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Check the wind every 10 minutes (Tip).</li><li>Move only when its head is down or behind cover (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full plan</summary><ul><li><strong>Nose:</strong> pick stands by the wind for the hour you sit. Have a plan B stand for a different wind (Tip).</li><li><strong>Nose:</strong> walk in on a route your scent will not cross the trail (Tip).</li><li><strong>Ears:</strong> quiet outer layer, tape metal on sling and pack (Tip).</li><li><strong>Ears:</strong> walk like a deer: step, step, stop (Tip).</li><li><strong>Eyes:</strong> shade, a background, slow hands (Tip).</li><li><strong>All three:</strong> arrive early and let the woods settle (Tip).</li><li>Deer urine lures from outside BC are banned for hunting (95%, synopsis page 12 item 51, via <a href=\"#/s/deer-mind\">How a deer thinks</a>). Wind beats lures anyway (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a deer with its field of view. Green covers about 310 degrees around it: it sees to the sides and almost behind without turning its head. A narrow orange wedge in front is where both eyes overlap and judge depth. A small brown wedge straight behind is the blind spot.\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">What a deer sees from one spot</text><path d=\"M200 160 L249.9 266.9 A 118 118 0 1 0 150.1 266.9 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" opacity=\".45\"/><path d=\"M200 160 L150.1 53.1 A 118 118 0 0 1 249.9 53.1 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".35\"/><path d=\"M200 160 L249.9 266.9 A 118 118 0 0 1 150.1 266.9 Z\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><g transform=\"translate(200 160)\"><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"24\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><ellipse cy=\"-26\" rx=\"8\" ry=\"12\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-7\" cy=\"-26\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/><circle cx=\"7\" cy=\"-26\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#23261f\"/></g><text x=\"200\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Both eyes: depth</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Side vision</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Side vision</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"268\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Blind behind</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">About 310 degrees without moving the head.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Nose knows, ears hear, eyes see what moves near.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 310 degrees, 4 to 8 kHz, 2 cones.</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (tradition): \"Hunt the wind, or hunt somewhere else.\"</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks, mistakes and field drill</summary><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Sun up, scent up. Sun down, scent down.\"</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule</strong> (widely taught, opinion): \"You can fool the eyes and the ears. You can never fool the nose.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 360 minus 310 = a 50 degree blind spot behind.</li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Sitting an evening stand above a river bottom: your scent drains down to them.</li><li>Unzipping a pack when a deer is in sight.</li><li>Turning your head quickly when you hear a step.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Next sit: hang a thread on your rifle. Note the wind direction every 10 minutes in the Journal, plus when it flips.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>Penn State Deer Research, <a href=\"https://www.deer.psu.edu/the-eyes-have-it/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The eyes have it</a>, search preview, checked 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li><li>Jacobs and others 1994, deer colour vision, via <code>research/2026-10-01-deer.md</code> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li>D'Angelo and others 2007, <a href=\"https://wildlife.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.2193/2006-326\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">deer hearing</a>, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li>Idaho Fish and Game, <a href=\"https://idfg.idaho.gov/sites/default/files/wildlife-express_sept-2017-whitetalied-deer.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wildlife Express: White tailed deer</a>, read 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li><li>BC <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/assets/gov/sports-recreation-arts-and-culture/outdoor-recreation/fishing-and-hunting/hunting/regulations/hunting-trapping-synopsis.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunting and Trapping Regulations Synopsis 2026 to 2028</a>, page 12 item 51, read directly 2026-10-02 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li>Research log: <code>research/2026-10-11-masterclass-white-tailed-deer.md</code>.</li></ul>"]